en</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Combined analysis of genome scans of dutch and finnish families reveals a susceptibility locus for high-density lipoprotein cholesterol on chromosome 16q</article-title><source>Am J Hum Genet</source><year>2003</year><volume>72</volume><fpage>903</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><comment>[Pajukanta, Paivi Allayee, Hooman Krass, Kelly L Kuraishy, Ali Soro, Aino Lilja, Heidi E Mar, Rebecca Taskinen, Marja-Riitta Nuotio, Ilpo Laakso, Markku Rotter, Jerome I de Bruin, Tjerk W A Cantor, Rita M Lusis, Aldons J Peltonen, Leena 5-t32-gm08243-15/gm/nigms Hl-28481/hl/nhlbi Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S. United States American journal of human genetics Am J Hum Genet. 2003 Apr;72(4):903&#x02013;17. Epub 2003 Mar 12.]</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12638083</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/374177</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Neyman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pearson</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the Problem of the Most Efficient Tests of Statistical Hypotheses</article-title><source>Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society of London Series A, Containing Papers of a Mathematical or Physical Character</source><year>1933</year><volume>231</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>337</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1098/rsta.1933.0009</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>